{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you've been having abdominal pain and vomiting. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I’ve had this pain for about two days now—diffuse, mostly in the lower belly. I’ve been nauseous and vomiting phlegm. I haven’t been able to keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’re not eating by mouth—you’re using your GJ tube for water and meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s right. I haven’t taken anything by mouth in years. I’ve been trying crushed prochlorperazine and ondansetron, but they’re not helping this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you’ve been using lorazepam and morphine for nausea and pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, but I get really sedated. Still, the pain and nausea don’t go away. This feels like my usual gastroparesis flares, but worse and not responding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You mentioned no diarrhea, fevers, or urinary symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, bowel movements are regular. No fever, chest pain, or shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks. In the ER, your white blood cell count was elevated—14.7—and you had some hematuria on urinalysis. But no signs of infection so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? The high white count?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s something we’re watching. But you don’t have fever or chills, and your blood cultures came back negative. So it may just be from inflammation or stress on the body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. What about the CT scan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT of your abdomen and pelvis showed no bowel obstruction or acute issue. No sign of another volvulus or blockage. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s probably just a bad gastroparesis flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what it looks like. We’ll manage your symptoms and make sure nothing else develops. We’ve started IV morphine and acetaminophen for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But morphine makes my stomach slower. Could that be making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent point. That’s exactly why we’re planning to taper the morphine and switch to tramadol, which is gentler on gastric motility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-11-17 00:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. The pain is still there, but not as intense. Nausea is still bothering me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reduced the IV morphine and started oral tramadol. We’re also continuing lorazepam for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe to restart tube feeds? I’m worried about making nausea worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We restarted low-dose tube feeds this morning. So far, you’re tolerating them well. We’ll gradually increase as your symptoms improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my white count—is it still high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 14.7 on admission, but it’s coming down. Today it’s 11.2. No infection found, so we think it’s resolving on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-11-18 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-11-18 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did a chest X-ray to check for pneumonia, since your white count was up. It was clear—no infection in the lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-11-18 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for checking. I’ve been worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You’re looking more comfortable today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel better. Pain is mild now, and I haven’t vomited since yesterday afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your white count is now 9.8—back to normal. We’re keeping you on tramadol and acetaminophen as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the nausea meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on lorazepam as needed. We’ve also added prochlorperazine for discharge, in case you need extra help at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’d like to avoid morphine if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-11-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’ll keep it as a backup, but tramadol is safer for your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-11-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—we had planned to replace your GJ tube this week. Since you’re here, interventional radiology can do it tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-11-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. I forgot about that. Is it necessary?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-11-19 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the tube is due for replacement. It’s a quick procedure with sedation. They’ll use imaging to guide it and make sure it’s placed correctly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-11-19 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your GJ tube was successfully replaced this morning. The new one is in place and ready to use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How did it go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smoothly. You got a little fentanyl for sedation, and the radiologist confirmed placement with contrast. No complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you. Your pain is well-controlled, nausea has improved, and labs are normal. You’re tolerating full tube feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What medications am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue your regular meds: citalopram, levothyroxine, omeprazole. For nausea, lorazepam and now prochlorperazine. For pain, tramadol every four hours as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And morphine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you a small supply—10 tablets—for severe pain only. But try to avoid it, as it can slow your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Please see your primary care provider this week to review everything and renew your prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-11-20 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad we could help. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-11-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—was the leukocytosis ever explained?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-11-20 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No clear infection was found. We believe the elevated white count was due to inflammation from your gastroparesis flare. It resolved without antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-11-20 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Thank you for explaining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-11-20 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nutrition team has confirmed your tube feeds are running smoothly. You’re getting full strength and tolerating it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-11-20 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ll keep that going at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-11-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge. Your vitals are stable—temperature 98.2, blood pressure 158/100, heart rate 88, oxygen 99% on room air."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-11-20 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "BP a bit high, but I’ve had that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-11-20 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we noted that. Keep monitoring it at home. Otherwise, you’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-11-20 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there anything else I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-11-20 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If nausea or pain returns and doesn’t respond to meds, or if you develop fever, vomiting, or tube issues, please call your doctor or go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-11-20 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-11-20 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge papers are ready. You’ll go home with home health services to help with GJ tube care for a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-11-20 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s helpful. I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-11-20 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you out shortly. Take care and get some rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-11-20 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel ready to go home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-11-17 00:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-11-20 18:23:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of gastroparesis, GJ tube placement, and prior cecal volvulus presented with a two-day history of diffuse abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting, consistent with a gastroparesis flare. She had elevated white blood cell count on admission but no signs of infection, and blood and urine cultures were negative. CT imaging showed no bowel obstruction or acute abdominal process. Pain was initially managed with IV morphine, but due to concerns about opioid-induced gastric slowing, she was transitioned to tramadol. Nausea was treated with lorazepam and tube feeds were successfully restarted. Her leukocytosis resolved spontaneously. As part of a planned outpatient procedure, her GJ tube was replaced by interventional radiology during the admission. She improved clinically, tolerated full tube feeds, and was discharged home with instructions to avoid opiates, continue new and home medications, and follow up with her primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Abdominal pain, other specified site",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Nausea alone",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Osteoporosis, unspecified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Personal history of other malignant neoplasm of skin"
    ]
  }
}
